From 69a16352c9b0b6591099f63a306238272db58b3a
Subject: compositor: check if 'cwindow_hash' is a valid pointer before use

Upstream: https://github.com/xfce-mirror/xfwm4/commit/69a16352c9b0b6591099f63a306238272db58b3a
Backport to the pinned Xfwm 4.20.0. With an external compositor,
compositorIsActive() may be true while the internal window hash is NULL.
Return the existing not-found result instead of calling GLib with NULL.
Remove this backport when the pinned upstream source includes the guard.

diff --git a/src/compositor.c b/src/compositor.c
--- a/src/compositor.c
+++ b/src/compositor.c
@@ -172,6 +172,11 @@ find_cwindow_in_screen (ScreenInfo *screen_info, Window id)
     g_return_val_if_fail (screen_info != NULL, NULL);
     TRACE ("window 0x%lx", id);
 
+    if (!screen_info->cwindow_hash)
+    {
+        return NULL;
+    }
+
     return g_hash_table_lookup(screen_info->cwindow_hash, (gpointer) id);
 }
 
